        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Pakistan’s prime minister says his nation is ready to facilitate talks to end Iran war Middle East Issued on: 24/03/2026 - 20:58 Pakistan’s prime minister says his country is ready to “facilitate meaningful and conclusive talks” to end the Iran war. Pakistan is one of the countries pushing diplomatically for talks between Iran and the United States after President Donald Trump said Monday there were ongoing negotiations between Washington and Tehran. FRANCE 24's August Hakansson reports. Saudi leader said to be pushing Trump to continue war in Iran, New York Times reports 24/03/2026 Middle East War on Iran: 'Fought on faulty assumptions, notion of externally delivered regime change delusional' 24/03/2026 Middle East Tension rises between Israel and Lebanon as IDF occupies south of Litani river 24/03/2026 Middle East Iran strikes put in question US-Israeli attacks's impact on military capabilities 24/03/2026 Middle East In Beirut, refugees stay put despite Israeli strikes 24/03/2026 Middle East 'We do not have a single war on Iran: We have an Israeli war and an American war' 24/03/2026 Middle East Israel and US interests diverge on possible negociation for end of war 24/03/2026 Middle East Israel's occupation of South Lebanon 'way to pressure Lebanese government' over Hezbollah 24/03/2026 Middle East Middle East war weighs heavy on Iranian population 24/03/2026 Middle East"
